IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`
IMPORT `tda-transfer`
IMPORT `tda-vehicles`
IMPORT `fhog-grant`
IMPORT `tda-seat`

-- Cases for the buyer's seat (tda-seat.l4): every exported question, asked as the buyer would, on plain answers. The
-- expected values were worked by hand from the deposited texts and agree with the core cases (tda-cases-transfer.l4,
-- tda-cases-vehicles.l4, fhog-cases-grant.l4), which show the arithmetic. HYPOTHETICAL buyers throughout. There is one
-- seat, so there are no mirror cases.
--
-- Argument orders (the seat's comments give them too):
--   first home buyer questions (27): transfer day, price, value, building on land, fixed and lawful, suitable, lived in
--     before, renovated-and-new, Help to Buy | my age, age exempted, citizen, owned before, grant before, Div 2A before,
--     exemption before, intend to live there | with another, their age, age exempted, citizen, owned, grant, Div 2A,
--     exemption, intend | the Commissioner's good reasons.
--   transfer duty (40): the 27 above, then PCC, Seniors Health Card, special rate pension, Div 2B before | selling a
--     Tasmanian home, its transfer day, its dutiable value, lived there 6 months before selling, before buying, same
--     names, another home | Division 2C off the plan, the day the contract was signed.
--   pensioner (22): the 9 transfer answers, my age, intend, PCC, SHC, special rate pension, Div 2B before, then the 7
--     former-home answers.

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Dutiable value, the general rate, joint tenants.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of my home` 480000 500000 EQUALS 500000
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the general rate` 500000 EQUALS 18247.50
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the general rate` 2500 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What share does each joint tenant hold for duty` 2 EQUALS 0.5

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- New or established; owner; spouse.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A house someone has lived in: established. Never lived in or sold: new. Vacant land: no home yet. Not lawfully
-- habitable: not a home.
#ASSERT `Which relief can apply to my home` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `an established home: the first home buyer duty exemption can apply (Duties Act s 57F(1)), and a contract made from 1 July 2014 to buy it cannot get the grant (FHOG Act s 13(1)(a), (ab))`
#ASSERT `Which relief can apply to my home` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a new home: the first home owner grant can apply (FHOG Act s 13(1)(ab)), and the duty exemption cannot (Duties Act s 57F(1))`
#ASSERT `Which relief can apply to my home` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a new home: the first home owner grant can apply (FHOG Act s 13(1)(ab)), and the duty exemption cannot (Duties Act s 57F(1))`
#ASSERT `Which relief can apply to my home` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no home on the land yet: a contract to build, or building as an owner builder, can get the grant (FHOG Act s 13(1)(b), (c)), and the duty exemption cannot (Duties Act s 57F(1))`
#ASSERT `Which relief can apply to my home` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not a home (FHOG Act s 4): neither the duty exemption nor the grant`
-- Freehold in land with a house: an owner of a home. The same freehold in vacant land: not. A Help to Buy interest of
-- Housing Australia: not.
#ASSERT `Does this interest make me an owner of a home` `an estate in fee simple` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT `Does this interest make me an owner of a home` `an estate in fee simple` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `Does this interest make me an owner of a home` `an interest of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (finding 9) A separated legal spouse: not a spouse for the grant, a spouse for the duty exemption.
#ASSERT (`Does this person count as my spouse` TRUE FALSE TRUE)'s `my spouse for the first home owner grant (FHOG Act s 6)` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Does this person count as my spouse` TRUE FALSE TRUE)'s `my spouse for the duty exemption (Duties Act s 3)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`Does this person count as my spouse` FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `my spouse for the first home owner grant (FHOG Act s 6)` EQUALS TRUE

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Am I an eligible first home buyer (s 57E)?
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Am I an eligible first home buyer` 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I am an eligible first home buyer (s 57E)`
-- On a temporary visa, buying with a citizen: eligible (s 57E(3)); alone: not.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible first home buyer` 28 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I am an eligible first home buyer (s 57E)`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible first home buyer` 28 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I am not an eligible first home buyer` `no transferee is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`
-- My spouse owned a home: not.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible first home buyer` 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I am not an eligible first home buyer` `a transferee or their spouse has previously been the owner of a home`
-- 17, exempted by the Commissioner: eligible.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible first home buyer` 17 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I am an eligible first home buyer (s 57E)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- The first home buyer duty exemption (27 answers).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Alex, 28, alone, established house, $500 000, transferred 1 March 2025: exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my home transfer exempt as a first home buyer` (YMD 2025 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the transfer is an eligible transaction`
-- (finding 1) The same, transferred 1 October 2026: outside the eligible period as deposited.
#ASSERT `Is my home transfer exempt as a first home buyer` (YMD 2026 10 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the transfer is outside the eligible period` (YMD 2024 2 18) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- With a partner whose spouse (a former husband) owned a home: not exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my home transfer exempt as a first home buyer` (YMD 2025 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 30 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a transferee is not an eligible first home buyer` `a transferee or their spouse has previously been the owner of a home`
-- (s 32) Under Help to Buy, transferred 10 June 2026 (after s 32 commenced on 5 June 2026), $600 000 full price:
-- Housing Australia is left out; exempt.
#ASSERT `Is my home transfer exempt as a first home buyer` (YMD 2026 6 10) 600000 600000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the transfer is an eligible transaction`
-- A new home: the exemption cannot apply.
#ASSERT `Is my home transfer exempt as a first home buyer` (YMD 2025 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the land has no established home on it`
-- Over the cap: $800 000 (the value, not the price, decides: a $740 000 price on an $800 000 property).
#ASSERT `Is my home transfer exempt as a first home buyer` (YMD 2025 3 1) 740000 800000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the dutiable value is over the cap` 750000

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- The 2018-2024 first home buyer concession (27 answers).
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Did my home transfer get the 2018-2024 first home buyer concession` (YMD 2022 3 1) 400000 400000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the transfer is an eligible transaction`
#ASSERT `Did my home transfer get the 2018-2024 first home buyer concession` (YMD 2025 3 1) 400000 400000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the transfer is outside the eligible period` (YMD 2018 2 7) (YMD 2024 6 30)
-- (finding 17) Transferred 1 March 2021, before the s 46D(1)(d) cap was last amended (1 January 2022): every other
-- requirement met, and the cap then in force is not deposited: not covered.
#ASSERT `Did my home transfer get the 2018-2024 first home buyer concession` (YMD 2021 3 1) 400000 400000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the transfer is dated before 1 January 2022, when the s 46D(1)(d) cap was last amended (No. 8 of 2022), and meets every other Division 2A requirement; the cap in force before then is not in the deposited consolidation`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- The pensioner duty concession (22 answers).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Pat, 67, PCC, sold the Hobart home ($750 000) on 1 March 2025, buys a $450 000 home transferred 1 May 2025: s 46N.
#ASSERT `Is the duty on my new home halved under the pensioner concession` (YMD 2025 5 1) 450000 450000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 67 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) 750000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the former home was transferred within 6 months before the purchase (s 46N)`
-- (finding 3) Sold 1 August 2026, bought 1 October 2026: the sale is outside the eligible period (ended 30 June 2025).
#ASSERT `Is the duty on my new home halved under the pensioner concession` (YMD 2026 10 1) 450000 450000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 67 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) 750000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no` (`the former home was not transferred within the eligible period` (YMD 2018 2 10) (YMD 2025 6 30))
-- A pensioner with a Veterans' Affairs special rate pension (no card), who sold after buying (s 46O).
#ASSERT `Is the duty on my new home halved under the pensioner concession` (YMD 2025 2 1) 450000 450000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 72 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) 750000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the former home was transferred within 6 months after the purchase (s 46O)`
-- No card or pension: not an eligible pensioner.
#ASSERT `Is the duty on my new home halved under the pensioner concession` (YMD 2025 5 1) 450000 450000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 67 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) 750000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no` `no transferee is an eligible pensioner (aged 60 or over, with a Pensioner Concession Card, Seniors Health Card or special rate pension, and no earlier Division 2B concession)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- What transfer duty must I pay (40 answers).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Alex, first home buyer, 1 March 2025, $500 000: nil.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2025 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 2 1) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0 `nil: the first home buyer duty exemption (s 57G)`
-- (finding 1) Alex, 1 October 2026: the general rate, 18 247.50.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2026 10 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 18247.50 `the general rate (s 29)`
-- Alex, a 2022 transfer at $400 000: half, 6 998.75.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2022 3 1) 400000 400000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2022 2 1) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 6998.75 `half the s 29 duty: the first home buyer duty concession (s 46E)`
-- Pat, pensioner, 1 May 2025, $450 000 after selling for $750 000 on 1 March 2025: half, 8 061.25.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2025 5 1) 450000 450000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 67 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) 750000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 4 1) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 8061.25 `half the s 29 duty: the pensioner duty concession (s 46N(3) or s 46O(3))`
-- A buyer on a temporary visa, alone, 1 October 2026: no relief, Part 3A not encoded.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2026 10 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1) EQUALS `not covered` `a transferee is a foreign person: Part 3A additional duty for foreign purchasers (and the s 30J exemption) is not encoded`
-- (finding 8) A citizen buying with a temporary visa holder, both first home buyers, 1 March 2025: nil.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2025 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 27 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 2 1) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0 `nil: the first home buyer duty exemption (s 57G)`
-- An off-the-plan strata unit under a contract signed 1 January 2026, in the Division 2C period: not covered.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2026 2 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS `not covered` `the home is a strata or conjoined dwelling bought before its occupancy permit was granted, under an agreement executed in the Division 2C eligible period (from 1 July 2024; to 30 June 2026 as deposited): the Division 2C pre-completion duty concession is not encoded`
-- (finding 18) The same off-the-plan unit under a contract signed 1 August 2026, after the Division 2C period ended
-- (30 June 2026), transferred 1 March 2027: Division 2C cannot reach it; a new home, so no exemption; the general
-- rate on $500 000, 18 247.50.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2027 3 1) 500000 500000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 18247.50 `the general rate (s 29)`
-- (finding 17) Alex, an established house at $400 000 transferred 1 March 2021: the Division 2A answer turns on a cap
-- not deposited, so the duty is not covered.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2021 3 1) 400000 400000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 28 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2021 2 1) EQUALS `not covered` `the transfer is dated before 1 January 2022, when the s 46D(1)(d) cap was last amended (No. 8 of 2022), and meets every other Division 2A requirement; the cap in force before then is not in the deposited consolidation`
-- A second home buyer, a new $750 000 home on 1 March 2025: the general rate, 28 935.
#ASSERT `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` (YMD 2025 3 1) 750000 750000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2000 1 1) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 2 1) EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 28935 `the general rate (s 29)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- After settlement (the duty exemption).
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `By what date must I lodge and pay the duty on my home` (YMD 2025 11 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `By what date must I lodge and pay the duty on my home` (YMD 2025 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 15
-- Transferred 1 March 2025, moving in 1 April 2025: move in by 1 March 2026; stay until at least 1 October 2025.
#ASSERT (`By when must I move in and how long must I stay, for the exemption` (YMD 2025 3 1) 12 6 (YMD 2025 4 1))'s `I must move in no later than` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`By when must I move in and how long must I stay, for the exemption` (YMD 2025 3 1) 12 6 (YMD 2025 4 1))'s `if I move in on the day I gave, I must stay and keep my interest until at least` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 1
-- An approved 18 months to move in: by 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT (`By when must I move in and how long must I stay, for the exemption` (YMD 2025 3 1) 18 6 (YMD 2026 6 1))'s `I must move in no later than` EQUALS YMD 2026 9 1
-- Failed on 2 March 2026 ($500 000 home): notice by 16 March 2026; the Commissioner may reassess 18 247.50; fine up to
-- 100 penalty units.
#ASSERT (`What must I do after failing the residence requirement for the exemption` (YMD 2026 3 2) 500000 500000)'s `I must give the Commissioner written notice no later than` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 16
#ASSERT (`What must I do after failing the residence requirement for the exemption` (YMD 2026 3 2) 500000 500000)'s `the duty the Commissioner may then reassess, in dollars` EQUALS 18247.50
#ASSERT (`What must I do after failing the residence requirement for the exemption` (YMD 2026 3 2) 500000 500000)'s `the most I can be fined for not giving notice, in penalty units` EQUALS 100

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- The first home owner grant.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Criteria (19 answers). Jordan, 25, alone: all met.
#ASSERT `Do we meet the grant's eligibility criteria` 25 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (finding 11) With a parent who owned and lived in a home: criterion 4.
#ASSERT `Do we meet the grant's eligibility criteria` 25 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 55 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `criterion 4: an applicant or spouse held and lived in residential property for 6 months before (s 11(3))`
-- An earlier grant in another State, paid back: met.
#ASSERT `Do we meet the grant's eligibility criteria` 30 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Eligible transaction (9 answers). A contract for a new home, 1 August 2026: eligible; for an established home: not.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction eligible for the grant` `a contract to buy a home` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my transaction eligible for the grant` `a contract to buy a home` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible transaction: a contract made from 1 July 2014 must be for a new home (s 13(1)(ab))`
-- A building contract on land the buyer will own.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction eligible for the grant` `a comprehensive home building contract` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an eligible transaction (s 13(1))`
-- A home in Victoria.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction eligible for the grant` `a contract to buy a home` FALSE (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible transaction: the home is not in Tasmania`

-- Joinder.
#ASSERT `Must this owner join my grant application` `a person who is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home` EQUALS `yes: they must join in my application (s 15)`
#ASSERT `Must this owner join my grant application` `Homes Tasmania (reg 5)` EQUALS `no: they are excluded from s 15`
#ASSERT `Must this owner join my grant application` `the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement (reg 5A, s 5(2A))` EQUALS `no: they are excluded from s 15`

-- Entitlement (36 answers). Jordan, alone, new townhouse, contract 1 August 2026, settled 1 December 2026: payable.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the first home owner grant` 25 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a contract to buy a home` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) TRUE 520000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the grant is payable (s 7)`
-- A parent on the title who does not apply: not payable.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the first home owner grant` 25 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `a contract to buy a home` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) TRUE 520000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not payable: an interested person has not joined in the application (s 15)`
-- Not yet settled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the first home owner grant` 25 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a contract to buy a home` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) FALSE 520000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not payable: the transaction has not been completed (s 7(1)(b)(ii))`

-- Amount (10 answers). Contract 1 August 2026, settled 1 December 2026: $20 000 (s 18M); 1 August 2025: $30 000 (s 18L);
-- 1 August 2024: $10 000 (finding 7).
#ASSERT `How much is my first home owner grant` `a contract to buy a home` (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) 520000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the grant, in dollars, is` 20000 "s 18(2)(am), s 18M"
#ASSERT `How much is my first home owner grant` `a contract to buy a home` (YMD 2025 8 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) 520000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the grant, in dollars, is` 30000 "s 18(2)(al), s 18L"
#ASSERT `How much is my first home owner grant` `a contract to buy a home` (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2025 3 1) 520000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the grant, in dollars, is` 10000 "s 18(2)(b)(ii)"
-- A building contract of 1 September 2026 completed 15 September 2028, more than 24 months on: $10 000.
#ASSERT `How much is my first home owner grant` `a comprehensive home building contract` (YMD 2026 9 1) (YMD 2028 9 15) 450000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the grant, in dollars, is` 10000 "s 18(2)(b)(ii)"

-- Application period: settled 1 December 2026, applying 15 January 2027: in time, period ends 1 December 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my grant application in time` (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE EQUALS `within the application period, which ends on` (YMD 2027 12 1)
#ASSERT `Is my grant application in time` (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2028 1 15) FALSE EQUALS `outside the application period: only if the Commissioner allows it (s 14(6))` (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2027 12 1)
#ASSERT `Is my grant application in time` (YMD 2026 8 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2028 1 15) TRUE EQUALS `outside the application period, but the Commissioner has allowed it (s 14(6))`

-- s 19(3): duty 19 097.50 on Jordan's $520 000 new townhouse; a $20 000 grant clears it with 902.50 left over.
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the general rate` 520000 EQUALS 19097.50
#ASSERT (`How much duty is left if my grant is applied to it` 19097.50 20000)'s `the duty left to pay, in dollars` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`How much duty is left if my grant is applied to it` 19097.50 20000)'s `the grant left to be paid to me, in dollars` EQUALS 902.50

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- After completion (a grant paid in anticipation).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Completed 1 December 2026, moving in 1 January 2027: move in by 1 December 2027; stay until at least 1 July 2027.
#ASSERT (`By when must I move in and how long must I stay, for the grant` (YMD 2026 12 1) 12 6 (YMD 2027 1 1))'s `I must move in no later than` EQUALS YMD 2027 12 1
#ASSERT (`By when must I move in and how long must I stay, for the grant` (YMD 2026 12 1) 12 6 (YMD 2027 1 1))'s `if I move in on the day I gave, I must stay and keep my interest until at least` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 1
-- It became apparent on 1 May 2027 that Jordan would not move in: notice and repayment by 15 May 2027; fine up to 100
-- penalty units.
#ASSERT (`By when must I tell the Commissioner and repay my grant` (YMD 2026 12 1) 12 6 (YMD 2027 5 1))'s `I must tell the Commissioner in writing and repay the grant no later than` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 15
#ASSERT (`By when must I tell the Commissioner and repay my grant` (YMD 2026 12 1) 12 6 (YMD 2027 5 1))'s `the most I can be fined, in penalty units` EQUALS 100
-- It never became apparent before the period ended (1 June 2028): by 15 June 2028.
#ASSERT (`By when must I tell the Commissioner and repay my grant` (YMD 2026 12 1) 12 6 (YMD 2028 7 1))'s `I must tell the Commissioner in writing and repay the grant no later than` EQUALS YMD 2028 6 15
-- Sold on 1 March 2027: by 15 March 2027; exempted joint applicant: nothing.
#ASSERT `By when must I repay my grant after giving up my interest` (YMD 2027 3 1) FALSE EQUALS `the applicant must give the Commissioner written notice and repay the grant no later than` (YMD 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT `By when must I repay my grant after giving up my interest` (YMD 2027 3 1) TRUE EQUALS `nothing: the Commissioner exempted the applicant from the residence requirement (s 12(2))`
-- s 38(3): $20 000 to repay, up to $20 000 penalty.
#ASSERT `What is the most penalty if I do not repay my grant` 20000 EQUALS 20000

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Registering a vehicle.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Who pays duty on my vehicle application` `a notice of a change of beneficial ownership` EQUALS `the person acquiring the beneficial ownership (s 195(b))`
#ASSERT `Who pays duty on my vehicle application` `an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration` EQUALS `no one: the application is not charged (s 192)`
-- A used sedan bought for $38 000, market value $37 000, transfer of registration on 24 October 2026: 1 050 + 11 x 30 =
-- 1 380.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 10 24) `an application to register a vehicle in a name or names different from its last registration` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 38000 37000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the vehicle duty, in dollars, is` 1380 `the passenger vehicle rate (s 197(2))`
-- A new ute (car-derived body) for $45 000, price accepted: 3 x 450 = 1 350 at the general rate.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 10 24) `an application to register a vehicle not previously registered under the Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 45000 45000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the vehicle duty, in dollars, is` 1350 `the general rate, $3 per $100 or part (s 197(1))`
-- A $400 trailer-towing runabout... a $400 car: $20.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 10 24) `an application to register a vehicle in a name or names different from its last registration` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400 400 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the vehicle duty, in dollars, is` 20 `the fixed $20 (s 197(3))`
-- Re-registering in the same name: no duty.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 10 24) `an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 38000 37000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no duty: the application is not charged (s 192)`
-- An exemption claimed: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` (YMD 2026 10 24) `an application to register a vehicle in a name or names different from its last registration` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 38000 37000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `an exemption under ss 199 to 203 is claimed for the vehicle: those exemptions are not encoded`
-- Dutiable value: a new car at $45 000 (market $47 000), price accepted: 45 000; not accepted: 47 000.
#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of my vehicle` TRUE 45000 47000 TRUE EQUALS 45000
#ASSERT `What is the dutiable value of my vehicle` TRUE 45000 47000 FALSE EQUALS 47000
-- The s 193(1) statement: owed with a charged application, not with a same-name re-registration.
#ASSERT `Must I lodge a statement of the dutiable value` `a notice of a change of beneficial ownership`
#ASSERT (NOT `Must I lodge a statement of the dutiable value` `an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration`)
